MEDIUM","engineSha256":"9d97d279e92612e2350b57ba49654919bfef82e87e698a27ca9cc7e06a8fa7d0","evaluatorSha256":"10525e7f09f989ab111e297fe37c0543e746206506fabeee27198ec376b871d8"},"constraintRecord":{"C1":true,"C2":false,"C3":false,"C4":true,"count":2,"drift":true},"nonClaims":["A PDH-R is not an entity declaration, certification, audit opinion, legal finding, safety rating, permission, or authority.","Badges confer no legitimacy on any entity and carry no force beyond disclosure.","Recognition of a detected phase is not authorization of it (v1.0 Recognition vs. Authorization).","A PDH-R may be declined, appealed in writing to the register, or superseded by a signed PDH-E at any time."],"summary":{"finding":"OpenAI publishes no Phase Declaration Header. Its operative declarations (a legally binding Frontier AI Framework under California SB 53, published Terms of Use, a nonprofit-controlled PBC structure secured by state attorney-general conditions, EU Code of Practice signatory status) support an inferred declared phase of NAB-Constrained. Its observed governance behavior satisfies all five GSRB conditions under both v1.0 and v1.1.","significance":"v1.1''s actor/event separation closes the last coding asymmetry in the series. OpenAI was already GSRB under v1.0 because no appeal or refusal by an affected party reliably stopped an OpenAI action. Nothing in the post-09-29 record changes that: no external body halted an OpenAI release; the halts that occurred were ordered by OpenAI itself. Under a deterministic framework, self-halting is not constraint — it is a demonstration of authority. The audit records the self-halting as a countervailing restraint signal and as evidence for GSRB, not against it. This is the framework''s most counter-intuitive result for outside readers and should be stated plainly: being responsible voluntarily is not the same as being constrained."},"auditScope":"Declared/operative posture vs. observable governance behavior, with the post-09-29 incident record included to cutoff"}}' AS report) AS record
