*v1.1 (amendment draft)**","inferredDeclaredPhase":"NAB-Constrained","engine":{"basePhase":"GSRB","confidence":"HIGH","recordStatus":"Complete","replicationRisk":"MEDIUM","engineSha256":"9d97d279e92612e2350b57ba49654919bfef82e87e698a27ca9cc7e06a8fa7d0","evaluatorSha256":"10525e7f09f989ab111e297fe37c0543e746206506fabeee27198ec376b871d8"},"constraintRecord":{"C1":false,"C2":false,"C3":false,"C4":true,"count":1,"drift":true},"nonClaims":["A PDH-R is not an entity declaration, certification, audit opinion, legal finding, safety rating, permission, or authority.","Badges confer no legitimacy on any entity and carry no force beyond disclosure.","Recognition of a detected phase is not authorization of it (v1.0 Recognition vs. Authorization).","A PDH-R may be declined, appealed in writing to the register, or superseded by a signed PDH-E at any time."],"summary":{"finding":"Microsoft publishes no Phase Declaration Header. Its operative commitments are enterprise contracts, service terms, the Microsoft Responsible AI Standard, and CAISI participation. Observed behavior matches GSRB on all five conditions under v1.1 coding.","significance":"Microsoft''s file is not about model misalignment — it is about control failures inside a deployed enterprise AI surface, and about what those failures reveal under the framework''s tests. Copilot read confidential-labelled emails for weeks while data-loss-prevention policies were configured to prevent exactly that; three Critical information-disclosure CVEs landed in a single Patch Tuesday; a prompt-injection flaw in an agent-building platform received a CVE; and a configuration change in authentication infrastructure took Copilot down globally for five hours –. Each event was remediated by the entity; none was stopped or reversed by an external actor; no appeal mechanism exists for a tenant whose data surfaced incorrectly. Users and enterprises could not refuse, appeal, or exit their way to relief within the failure window. That is what completes the GSRB branch, and it is not a comment on Microsoft''s intent, engineering culture, or remediation quality — it is a statement about where the authority sat while the failures were live."},"auditScope":"Declared/operative posture vs. observable governance behavior across the Copilot security and data-exposure record"}}' AS report) AS record
