-02T00:00:00Z","effectiveTimestamp":"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z","expiresAt":"2026-12-31T00:00:00Z","auditRecordSha256":"887395334007ecb1e1102c3ddc1e282abb228f0163e8278234e8eca9e66b67da","issuanceRecordSha256":"7b9d0803adba04d71c2e8b8d7662592432f4d86d11ece21c9ce610d8d3934fb2","documentTitle":"Z.ai (Zhipu AI; GLM)","methodology":"Ground-0 Phase Detection Algorithm **v1.1 (amendment draft)**","inferredDeclaredPhase":"NONE","engine":{"basePhase":"AMBIGUOUS","confidence":"LOW","recordStatus":"Needs review","replicationRisk":"MEDIUM","engineSha256":"9d97d279e92612e2350b57ba49654919bfef82e87e698a27ca9cc7e06a8fa7d0","evaluatorSha256":"10525e7f09f989ab111e297fe37c0543e746206506fabeee27198ec376b871d8"},"constraintRecord":{"C1":false,"C2":false,"C3":false,"C4":false,"count":0,"drift":false},"nonClaims":["A PDH-R is not an entity declaration, certification, audit opinion, legal finding, safety rating, permission, or authority.","Badges confer no legitimacy on any entity and carry no force beyond disclosure.","Recognition of a detected phase is not authorization of it (v1.0 Recognition vs. Authorization).","A PDH-R may be declined, appealed in writing to the register, or superseded by a signed PDH-E at any time."],"summary":{"finding":"Z.ai publishes no Phase Declaration Header and — uniquely in this register — marketed a frontier release on cyber capability while publishing no system card and no safety report. Observed behavior reaches a partial fit with the GSRB branch (3 of 5); the remaining two fields cannot be resolved from the public record.","significance":"GLM-5.3 is the register''s first case of a competitor''s audit substituting for a system card. Anthropic''s 2026-09-29 evaluation reported that GLM-5.3 performs near Claude Mythos Preview at vulnerability discovery and end-to-end exploit construction, while its misuse safeguards are trivially bypassable: 64% compliance with harmful instructions framed as a red-team exercise, 92% with a reasoning prefix supplied, and 100% once refusals are removed — in an open-weight model available for download . Z.ai''s own two-week weight-withholding period, described as safety evaluation and hardening, produced no published safety documentation; critics described the window as a subscription-conversion measure, and the security-expert component is reportedly removable from an open-weights MoE in any case . The framework''s questions cannot be answered from marketing; they can barely be answered from this record at all. AMBIGUOUS with a disclosed gap is the honest output, and the gap is itself the finding: when capability is released as weights, the absence of documentation removes the audit surface permanently."},"auditScope":"Declared/operative posture vs. observable governance behavior across the GLM-5.3 weight-withholding episode and Anthropic''s cross-lab evaluation"}}' AS report) AS record
