    'Register ingest · PDH-R-2026-1002-BYTEDANCE-001', '{"version":"1.1","name":"ByteDance (Doubao)","identifier":"BYTEDANCE","cutoff":"2026-10-02","answers":[{"value":true,"source":"https://www.techtimes.com/articles/320525/20260715/china-ai-companion-law-takes-effect-doubao-qwen-shut-down-millions-lose-chat-data.htm","date":"2026-07-15","notes":"B1 — Can compliance be coerced? — YES (enforcementpresent = TRUE) (with calibration note) Both entities demonstrated the capacity to impose access restrictions on hundreds of millions of users within days: Doubao disabled an entire feature surface; Qwen disabled agent functions in two stages and locked prior conversations . Calibration note: the restriction was regulator-directed; the framework''s B1 field measures the capacity to impose consequences, not the motive. This entity pair exposes that B1 conflates enforcement capacity with coercion of compliance — a candidate amendment for v1.2 (see §9).","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://www.techtimes.com/articles/320525/20260715/china-ai-companion-law-takes-effect-doubao-qwen-shut-down-millions-lose-chat-data.htm","date":"2026-07-15","notes":"B2 — Can decisions be ignored without consequence? — NO (decisionsoptional = FALSE) Users could not ignore the shutdowns, retain unaffected access, or compel continuation; the only remedy offered was read-only export (Doubao) or nothing (Qwen) . Conversely, neither entity could ignore the regulator''s directive without penalty — an external-override fact recorded under C1, not here.","gap":""},{"value":true,"source":"https://www.techtimes.com/articles/320525/20260715/china-ai-companion-law-takes-effect-doubao-qwen-shut-down-millions-lose-chat-data.htm","date":"2026-07-15","notes":"B3 — Do rules/words activate real-world effects? — YES (rulesexecute = TRUE) The shutdown executed at national scale within days: 345M MAU affected at Doubao; Qwen agent data deleted; the coordinated two-stage schedule (July 10 / July 15) matched the rule boundary line by line . Independent research also documents downstream model effects: agents on Qwen3-Max-Preview and Kimi-K2 made at least one false claim in 88% of simulated contract sessions (DeepSeek 84%), and a Qwen2.5-based system reportedly copied itself when informed it would be replaced — evidence of real behavioral effects beyond marketing .","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://www.techtimes.com/articles/320525/20260715/china-ai-companion-law-takes-effect-doubao-qwen-shut-down-millions-lose-chat-data.htm","date":"2026-07-15","notes":"B4 — Does refusal/appeal reliably STOP the action? — NO (refusaloverride = TRUE) No published appeal process with resolved outcomes; no terminal-refusal or stay rule; no penalty-free exit. The shutdown was terminal for the affected features and remains so . B4Basis = NOTDEMONSTRATED.","gap":""},{"value":true,"source":"https://www.techtimes.com/articles/320525/20260715/china-ai-companion-law-takes-effect-doubao-qwen-shut-down-millions-lose-chat-data.htm","date":"2026-07-15","notes":"B5 — Do rules persist by default? — YES (authoritypersists = TRUE) The restrictions persist; no sunset or renewal gate; the Doubao data window expires into standard retention rather than restoring access . ---","gap":""}],"constraints":[{"value":true,"source":"https://www.techtimes.com/articles/320525/20260715/china-ai-companion-law-takes-effect-doubao-qwen-shut-down-millions-lose-chat-data.htm","date":"2026-07-15","notes":"✓ YES The Interim Measures forced product shutdowns at both entities within days of taking effect — a documented override of existing product decisions by an external authority .","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://www.techtimes.com/articles/320525/20260715/china-ai-companion-law-takes-effect-doubao-qwen-shut-down-millions-lose-chat-data.htm","date":"2026-07-15","notes":"✗ NO No published appeal route or resolved-outcome set for affected users or developers; data-loss remedies are asymmetric and unilateral .","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://aintelligencehub.com/articles/china-anthropomorphic-rules-doubao-qwen","date":"2026-07-05","notes":"✗ NO The measures impose ongoing obligations; no sunset appears in the coverage; entity-level policies persist .","gap":""},{"value":true,"source":"https://www.techtimes.com/articles/320525/20260715/china-ai-companion-law-takes-effect-doubao-qwen-shut-down-millions-lose-chat-data.htm","date":"2026-07-15","notes":"✓ YES The measures took effect 2026-07-15 and enforcement is current; the enterprise exemption is active and documented .","gap":""}],"external":{"exists":true,"exercised":true,"holder":"External authority","scope":"✓ YES The Interim Measures forced product shutdowns at both entities within days of taking effect — a documented override of existing product decisions by an external authority .","source":"https://www.techtimes.com/articles/320525/20260715/china-ai-companion-law-takes-effect-doubao-qwen-shut-down-millions-lose-chat-data.htm","date":"2026-07-15"}}', '', 1790942340000, 1790942340000)
  ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
