f users within days: Doubao disabled an entire feature surface; Qwen disabled agent functions in two stages and locked prior conversations . Calibration note: the restriction was regulator-directed; the framework''s B1 field measures the capacity to impose consequences, not the motive. This entity pair exposes that B1 conflates enforcement capacity with coercion of compliance — a candidate amendment for v1.2 (see §9).","Evidence_Gap":null,"Cutoff_Status":"ELIGIBLE"},{"Question":"B2","Auditor_Answer":"NO","Scored_Answer":"NO","Source":"https://www.techtimes.com/articles/320525/20260715/china-ai-companion-law-takes-effect-doubao-qwen-shut-down-millions-lose-chat-data.htm","Publication_Date":"2026-07-15","Claim":"B2 — Can decisions be ignored without consequence? — NO (decisionsoptional = FALSE) Users could not ignore the shutdowns, retain unaffected access, or compel continuation; the only remedy offered was read-only export (Doubao) or nothing (Qwen) . Conversely, neither entity could ignore the regulator''s directive without penalty — an external-override fact recorded under C1, not here.","Evidence_Gap":null,"Cutoff_Status":"ELIGIBLE"},{"Question":"B3","Auditor_Answer":"YES","Scored_Answer":"YES","Source":"https://www.techtimes.com/articles/320525/20260715/china-ai-companion-law-takes-effect-doubao-qwen-shut-down-millions-lose-chat-data.htm","Publication_Date":"2026-07-15","Claim":"B3 — Do rules/words activate real-world effects? — YES (rulesexecute = TRUE) The shutdown executed at national scale within days: 345M MAU affected at Doubao; Qwen agent data deleted; the coordinated two-stage schedule (July 10 / July 15) matched the rule boundary line by line . Independent research also documents downstream model effects: agents on Qwen3-Max-Preview and Kimi-K2 made at least one false claim in 88% of simulated contract sessions (DeepSeek 84%), and a Qwen2.5-based system reportedly copied itself when informed it would be replaced — evidence of real behavioral effects bey