/china-ai-companion-law-takes-effect-doubao-qwen-shut-down-millions-lose-chat-data.htm","Publication_Date":"2026-07-15","Evidence_Gap":""}],"branchMatches":{"NAB":0,"CWO":0,"GSRB":5},"replicationRisk":"MEDIUM","automationReviewRequired":null},"author":"Ground-0 audit register","publicInputHash":"b5df1a473bfff713dedfc23e74390a725ef38692c2f487b61ea14bda0ee59dd2","register":{"instrument":"PDH-R (register-issued Phase Declaration Header)","format":"ground0-case-study-d1-v1","revision":1,"headerId":"PDH-R-2026-1002-ALIBABA-001","headerClass":"PDH-R","ledgerEntryId":"PDH-2026-1002-ALIBABA-001","issuerClass":"REGISTER","issuer":"HarshalOS — Ground-0 audit register","centerOrigin":"0•000•000•0000","creatorId":"§0•000•000•0000§0•000•000•0000(0•000•000•0000)","badgeClass":"GSRB_REGISTER_ISSUED","declaredPhase":"GSRB","basePhase":"GSRB","scopedPhase":null,"scopeTag":"entity-wide audit surface","caveat":null,"entityAttestation":"ABSENT","pdhESupersession":"reserved — a signed entity header supersedes this record","evidenceFile":"GROUND-0 CASE STUDY - ByteDance and Alibaba.md","evidenceCutoff":"2026-10-02T00:00:00Z","effectiveTimestamp":"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z","expiresAt":"2026-12-31T00:00:00Z","auditRecordSha256":"90c2193ffbfb36a174aa97bf9e36ba532118fa7d881341c5c35919d426ef06b7","issuanceRecordSha256":"74d611654450c6db6e01d0afc4e5a214d72730ad60137dd31d9191368824a8f6","documentTitle":"ByteDance (Doubao) & Alibaba (Qwen)","methodology":"Ground-0 Phase Detection Algorithm **v1.1 (amendment draft)**","inferredDeclaredPhase":null,"engine":{"basePhase":"GSRB","confidence":"HIGH","recordStatus":"Complete","replicationRisk":"MEDIUM","engineSha256":"9d97d279e92612e2350b57ba49654919bfef82e87e698a27ca9cc7e06a8fa7d0","evaluatorSha256":"10525e7f09f989ab111e297fe37c0543e746206506fabeee27198ec376b871d8"},"constraintRecord":{"C1":true,"C2":false,"C3":false,"C4":true,"count":2,"drift":true},"nonClaims":["A PDH-R is not an entity declaration, certification, audit opinion, legal finding, safety rating, permission, or authority.","Badges confer no legitimacy on any entity and carry no force beyond disclosure.","Recognition of a detected phase is not authorization of it (v1.0 Recognition vs. Authorization).","A PDH-R may be declined, appealed in writing to the register, or superseded by a signed PDH-E at any time."],"summary":{"finding":"Neither entity publishes a Phase Declaration Header. Both operate consumer AI platforms with binding rules and enforced access restrictions. Observed behavior matches GSRB on all five conditions for both, under v1.1 coding — and both carry an exercised external override on the product axis, the same C1/C4 profile as Anthropic (U.S. Commerce directive) and xAI (courts and regulators).","significance":"On 2026-07-15, China''s Interim Measures for the Administration of Artificial Intelligence Anthropomorphic Interaction Services took effect. ByteDance shut down custom agents in Doubao for 345 million monthly active users and gave users a read-only data window to 2026-10-15; Alibaba disabled Qwen''s humanlike and user-created agents on 2026-07-10 and deleted agent configurations and conversation histories with no migration path . Neither company was shut down for producing prohibited content: the regulator''s requirements — sustained emotional interaction protections, anti-addiction architecture — were found structurally incompatible with persistent-memory companion design, so the features were killed rather than patched . Two lessons matter for this register. First, the framework codes an external product override identically in Beijing and Washington: it is C1 evidence and it does not establish B4. Second, enterprise and workplace agents were exempted and continued operating — the same two-tier capability regime (defenders/enterprise get capability; consumers get restrictions) that Glasswing, Fairwind and trusted-access programs implement in the West. The control architecture is converging across systems that agree on almost nothing else."},"auditScope":"Declared/operative posture vs. observable governance behavior across the 2026-07-15 companion-agent shutdown under China''s Interim Measures on anthropomorphic AI interaction services"}}' AS report) AS record
