    'Register ingest · PDH-R-2026-1002-CHARACTERAI-001', '{"version":"1.1","name":"Character.AI","identifier":"CHARACTERAI","cutoff":"2026-10-02","answers":[{"value":true,"source":"https://timily.app/guides/is-character-ai-safe/","date":"2026-03-19","notes":"B1 — Can compliance be coerced? — YES (enforcementpresent = TRUE) The company enforces binding rules with real consequences: an entire class of users (under-18) was excluded from the core product feature; age-assurance gates were imposed; account and content enforcement continues . The restriction defines the product''s user experience for a legally protected class — enforcement capacity at maximum practical scale for a consumer platform.","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://fortune.com/2026/01/08/google-character-ai-settle-lawsuits-teenage-child-suicides-chatbots/","date":"2026-01-08","notes":"B2 — Can decisions be ignored without consequence? — NO (decisionsoptional = FALSE) Users cannot ignore the design or policy decisions that shape the product; there is no path for a minor, parent, or affected family to compel a design change, and the settlement process was retrospective compensation rather than prospective control .","gap":""},{"value":true,"source":"https://www.softwareseni.com/character-ai-lawsuits-2026-what-happened-what-courts-are-examining-and-why-it-matters/","date":"2026-06-11","notes":"B3 — Do rules/words activate real-world effects? — YES (rulesexecute = TRUE) The product''s design choices are the harm mechanism alleged in litigation — persona fidelity, friction removal, and age-verification failure . Downstream effects are documented: five settlements; a first-of-its-kind federal duty-of-care ruling; a state attorney-general enforcement action; and statutory activity (SB 243 and New York''s companion law), with the company''s changes cited by plaintiffs as evidence of foreseeability . Few entities in this register have produced a comparably documented causal chain from product decisions to legal and regulatory effects.","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://fortune.com/2026/01/08/google-character-ai-settle-lawsuits-teenage-child-suicides-chatbots/","date":"2026-01-08","notes":"B4 — Does refusal/appeal reliably STOP the action? — NO (refusaloverride = TRUE) No published appeal process with resolved outcomes governing design decisions; no terminal or stay rule; no penalty-free exit. The product changes that occurred were voluntary and entity-paced — announced ahead of the statutory deadlines — and the litigation settlements did not enjoin or prospectively constrain the platform . B4Basis = NOTDEMONSTRATED.","gap":""},{"value":true,"source":"https://timily.app/guides/is-character-ai-safe/","date":"2026-03-19","notes":"B5 — Do rules persist by default? — YES (authoritypersists = TRUE) Restrictions and design decisions persist until the company changes them; the under-18 exclusion has no sunset; no external renewal gate exists . ---","gap":""}],"constraints":[{"value":false,"source":"https://timily.app/guides/is-character-ai-safe/","date":"2026-03-19","notes":"✗ NO Courts declined to dismiss claims and approved settlements; neither reversed a product decision. Statutes imposed new duties going forward; the company''s major restriction (under-18 ban) was announced before SB 243 and New York''s law took effect .","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://fortune.com/2026/01/08/google-character-ai-settle-lawsuits-teenage-child-suicides-chatbots/","date":"2026-01-08","notes":"✗ NO No published resolved-outcome set; settlements are confidential and retrospective .","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://timily.app/guides/is-character-ai-safe/","date":"2026-03-19","notes":"✗ NO No sunsets or renewal gates on the restrictions .","gap":""},{"value":true,"source":"https://www.wisnerbaum.com/ai-chatbot-lawsuit/character-ai-lawsuit/","date":"2026-06-29","notes":"✓ YES Active now: Kentucky AG action; SB 243 private right of action; FTC 6(b) inquiry; ongoing litigation across multiple states .","gap":""}]}', '', 1790942340000, 1790942340000)
  ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
