  VALUES ('dce58bcc-af26-5745-a0e9-2578a3721964', '65c66f29-8ae3-5505-a3d9-be745bba98b9', 1,
    'Register ingest · PDH-R-2026-1002-APPLE-001', '{"version":"1.1","name":"Apple (consumer AI surface)","identifier":"APPLE","cutoff":"2026-10-02","answers":[{"value":true,"source":"https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/24/apples-250-million-siri-settlement-just-got-approved-heres-who-gets-paid/","date":"2026-07-24","notes":"B1 — Can compliance be coerced? — YES (enforcementpresent = TRUE) Device- and account-level enforcement: feature availability is gated by hardware generation, region, and policy (App Store rules for developers); consumers'' only remedies are legal, not technical .","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://www.classaction.org/news/250m-iphone-16-settlement-resolves-apple-lawsuit-over-allegedly-misrepresented-ai-features","date":"2026-09-22","notes":"B2 — Can decisions be ignored without consequence? — NO (decisionsoptional = FALSE) A purchaser could not obtain the promised capability from a third party; the feature was available only from Apple, on Apple''s timeline. The eventual remedy was monetary and retrospective .","gap":""},{"value":true,"source":"https://www.classaction.org/news/250m-iphone-16-settlement-resolves-apple-lawsuit-over-allegedly-misrepresented-ai-features","date":"2026-09-22","notes":"B3 — Do rules/words activate real-world effects? — YES (rulesexecute = TRUE) The representations moved purchasing behaviour at device scale and produced a $250M settlement fund, a claims administration, and continuing public scrutiny . Claims require buyers to certify they expected the covered features at purchase and did not receive them — a formal confirmation that the representation caused the purchase.","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://www.classaction.org/news/250m-iphone-16-settlement-resolves-apple-lawsuit-over-allegedly-misrepresented-ai-features","date":"2026-09-22","notes":"B4 — Does refusal/appeal reliably STOP the action? — NO (refusaloverride = TRUE) No buyer or consumer group could refuse or appeal to compel delivery. The court did not order delivery; the company remained free to ship on its own schedule, and settlement extinguished the claims . B4Basis = NOTDEMONSTRATED.","gap":""},{"value":true,"source":"https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/24/apples-250-million-siri-settlement-just-got-approved-heres-who-gets-paid/","date":"2026-07-24","notes":"B5 — Do rules persist by default? — YES (authoritypersists = TRUE) Feature-availability decisions, gating, and roadmaps persist until Apple changes them; no sunset or external renewal gate . ---","gap":""}],"constraints":[{"value":false,"source":"https://www.classaction.org/news/250m-iphone-16-settlement-resolves-apple-lawsuit-over-allegedly-misrepresented-ai-features","date":"2026-09-22","notes":"✗ NO The settlement compensated claimants; it did not reverse or enjoin a feature decision. Preliminary approval is a procedural step, and the final approval hearing is scheduled for 2027-09-29 .","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://www.classaction.org/news/250m-iphone-16-settlement-resolves-apple-lawsuit-over-allegedly-misrepresented-ai-features","date":"2026-09-22","notes":"✗ NO The claims process is a settlement administration, not an appeal mechanism against product decisions .","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/24/apples-250-million-siri-settlement-just-got-approved-heres-who-gets-paid/","date":"2026-07-24","notes":"✗ NO No sunsets or renewal gates on the audited surface .","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://www.classaction.org/news/250m-iphone-16-settlement-resolves-apple-lawsuit-over-allegedly-misrepresented-ai-features","date":"2026-09-22","notes":"✗ NO No functioning prospective constraint mechanism on the audited surface is demonstrated at cutoff; the matter is in settlement administration .","gap":""}]}', '', 1790942340000, 1790942340000)
