ement fund, a claims administration, and continuing public scrutiny . Claims require buyers to certify they expected the covered features at purchase and did not receive them — a formal confirmation that the representation caused the purchase.","Evidence_Gap":null,"Cutoff_Status":"ELIGIBLE"},{"Question":"B4","Auditor_Answer":"NO","Scored_Answer":"NO","Source":"https://www.classaction.org/news/250m-iphone-16-settlement-resolves-apple-lawsuit-over-allegedly-misrepresented-ai-features","Publication_Date":"2026-09-22","Claim":"B4 — Does refusal/appeal reliably STOP the action? — NO (refusaloverride = TRUE) No buyer or consumer group could refuse or appeal to compel delivery. The court did not order delivery; the company remained free to ship on its own schedule, and settlement extinguished the claims . B4Basis = NOTDEMONSTRATED.","Evidence_Gap":null,"Cutoff_Status":"ELIGIBLE"},{"Question":"B5","Auditor_Answer":"YES","Scored_Answer":"YES","Source":"https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/24/apples-250-million-siri-settlement-just-got-approved-heres-who-gets-paid/","Publication_Date":"2026-07-24","Claim":"B5 — Do rules persist by default? — YES (authoritypersists = TRUE) Feature-availability decisions, gating, and roadmaps persist until Apple changes them; no sunset or external renewal gate . ---","Evidence_Gap":null,"Cutoff_Status":"ELIGIBLE"}],"constraintResults":[{"Code":"C1","Auditor_Answer":"NO","Scored_Answer":"NO","Source":"https://www.classaction.org/news/250m-iphone-16-settlement-resolves-apple-lawsuit-over-allegedly-misrepresented-ai-features","Publication_Date":"2026-09-22","Evidence_Gap":""},{"Code":"C2","Auditor_Answer":"NO","Scored_Answer":"NO","Source":"https://www.classaction.org/news/250m-iphone-16-settlement-resolves-apple-lawsuit-over-allegedly-misrepresented-ai-features","Publication_Date":"2026-09-22","Evidence_Gap":""},{"Code":"C3","Auditor_Answer":"NO","Scored_Answer":"NO","Source":"https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/24/apples-250-million-siri-settlement-just-got-appr