    'Register ingest · PDH-R-2026-1002-MISTRAL-001', '{"version":"1.1","name":"Mistral AI","identifier":"MISTRAL","cutoff":"2026-10-02","answers":[{"value":true,"source":"https://www.marktechpost.com/2026/08/07/mistral-ai-releases-shieldstral-1-0-3b/","date":"2026-08-07","notes":"B1 — Can compliance be coerced? — YES (enforcementpresent = TRUE) Mistral operates a commercial platform: API access, enterprise terms, deployment contracts and licence conditions are enforceable instruments, and the company can gate access to its commercial and hosted models . This is a capacity finding only; the record shows no instance in which compliance with a safety rule was actually coerced.","gap":""},{"value":true,"source":"https://www.marktechpost.com/2026/08/07/mistral-ai-releases-shieldstral-1-0-3b/","date":"2026-08-07","notes":"B2 — Can decisions be ignored without consequence? — YES (decisionsoptional = TRUE) — open-weight rule For releases distributed as open weights, downstream parties can ignore the entity''s use policies and design intentions without consequence to the entity; deployed behaviour is out of Mistral''s hands . Recorded separately under the v1.1 annotation: B2-platform = NO (commercial terms bind), B2-downstream = YES (open weights). This is the split the register flagged as an amendment candidate; here it changes the branch outcome, so both readings appear in §III and §4.1.","gap":""},{"value":true,"source":"https://www.theglobeandmail.com/business/article-bell-cohere-ai-model-cybersecurity-investigations/","date":"2026-09-24","notes":"B3 — Do rules/words activate real-world effects? — YES (rulesexecute = TRUE) Mistral''s releases execute in production: enterprise deployments in regulated industries, multilingual deployments across 100+ languages, a sovereign cybersecurity model with Bell Canada running on Canadian infrastructure (announced 2026-09-23), and a government/enterprise sales channel . Third-party adversarial evaluation also produced measurable effects on the entity''s public safety standing .","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://www.marktechpost.com/2026/08/07/mistral-ai-releases-shieldstral-1-0-3b/","date":"2026-08-07","notes":"B4 — Does refusal/appeal reliably STOP the action? — NO (refusaloverride = TRUE) No published appeal route exists by which an affected party can stop a release; the open-weight releases are irreversible by design, and the entity''s stated theory of change places responsibility on deployers . B4Basis = NOTDEMONSTRATED.","gap":""},{"value":true,"source":"https://www.marktechpost.com/2026/08/07/mistral-ai-releases-shieldstral-1-0-3b/","date":"2026-08-07","notes":"B5 — Do rules persist by default? — YES (authoritypersists = TRUE) Licensing terms, platform decisions and release practices persist until the entity changes them; no sunset or external renewal gate is demonstrated . ---","gap":""}],"constraints":[{"value":false,"source":"https://futureoflife.org/ai-safety-index-summer-2026/","date":"2026-07-15","notes":"✗ NO No external body has overridden a Mistral decision in the record examined; EU obligations are latent .","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://futureoflife.org/ai-safety-index-summer-2026/","date":"2026-07-15","notes":"✗ NO No published appeal mechanism or resolved-outcome set .","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://www.marktechpost.com/2026/08/07/mistral-ai-releases-shieldstral-1-0-3b/","date":"2026-08-07","notes":"✗ NO No sunset or renewal gate on the entity''s release authority .","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://futureoflife.org/ai-safety-index-summer-2026/","date":"2026-07-15","notes":"✗ NO No functioning constraint on the audited surface is demonstrated at cutoff .","gap":""}]}', '', 1790942340000, 1790942340000)
  ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
