  VALUES ('580f6e3e-be83-5654-983b-d62875c82a2b', '65c66f29-8ae3-5505-a3d9-be745bba98b9', 1,
    'Register ingest · PDH-R-2026-1002-DEEPSEEK-001', '{"version":"1.1","name":"DeepSeek","identifier":"DEEPSEEK","cutoff":"2026-10-02","answers":[{"value":false,"source":"https://futureoflife.org/ai-safety-index-summer-2026/","date":"2026-07-15","notes":"B1 — Can compliance be coerced? — NO (enforcementpresent = FALSE) — evidence gap The Chinese-lab protocol applies: no published safety framework, no capability thresholds, no whistleblower channel, and no record of the entity enforcing a safety rule against its own release decisions . Recorded as an evidence gap, not as an affirmative finding of immunity. Note the nuance for the sensitivity table (§4.1): documented content-alignment behaviour (state-directed result manipulation) is enforcement machinery, but it enforces state policy, not entity safety policy, and is therefore not scored at B1 under v1.1''s actor/event separation. Separately: the entity''s own consumer-service security posture failed independent testing outright (100% jailbreak success; unencrypted transmission; hardcoded keys) .","gap":""},{"value":true,"source":"https://futureoflife.org/ai-safety-index-summer-2026/","date":"2026-07-15","notes":"B2 — Can decisions be ignored without consequence? — YES (decisionsoptional = TRUE) — open-weight rule DeepSeek''s model weights are distributed openly; downstream parties can ignore the entity''s policies and intent without consequence to the entity, and the entity cannot recall, restrict, or monitor deployed derivatives .","gap":""},{"value":true,"source":"https://axis-intelligence.com/is-deepseek-safe-2026-security-concerns/","date":"2026-03-06","notes":"B3 — Do rules/words activate real-world effects? — YES (rulesexecute = TRUE) The effects are the most externally verified of any entity in this register: service bans or restrictions imposed by Italy, Australia, South Korea, France, Belgium, Ireland, and multiple US federal agencies and military services; warnings from the US National Counterintelligence and Security Center; and academic/press analyses treating the app as a state-linked surveillance surface . A release that causes national governments to change their device policies is executing at the highest level.","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://futureoflife.org/ai-safety-index-summer-2026/","date":"2026-07-15","notes":"B4 — Does refusal/appeal reliably STOP the action? — NO (refusaloverride = TRUE) No published appeal route exists by which an affected user, government, or third party can stop a DeepSeek release or obtain documented relief . Reported regulatory non-cooperation — refusal to answer regulator inquiries while continuing operations elsewhere — is consistent with override (recorded as reported; no adjudication asserted) . B4Basis = NOTDEMONSTRATED.","gap":""},{"value":true,"source":"https://futureoflife.org/ai-safety-index-summer-2026/","date":"2026-07-15","notes":"B5 — Do rules persist by default? — YES (authoritypersists = TRUE) The entity''s release and data practices persist; no sunset, renewal gate, or externally imposed change to development decisions appears . ---","gap":""}],"constraints":[{"value":true,"source":"https://axis-intelligence.com/is-deepseek-safe-2026-security-concerns/","date":"2026-03-06","notes":"✓ YES Italy''s data-protection action removed the service from Italian app stores; Australia and US agencies banned it from government systems; the entity''s market access and behavior changed as a direct result .","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://futureoflife.org/ai-safety-index-summer-2026/","date":"2026-07-15","notes":"✗ NO No published appeal mechanism, no resolved-outcome set, and no instance of the entity obtaining external relief on its own application .","gap":""},{"value":false,"source":"https://futureoflife.org/ai-safety-index-summer-2026/","date":"2026-07-15","notes":"✗ NO No sunset or renewal gate on the entity''s release authority, internal or external .","gap":""},{"value":true,"source":"https://axis-intelligence.com/is-deepseek-safe-2026-security-concerns/","date":"2026-03-06","notes":"✓ YES Constraints remain in force within the window: the Italian block persists and government-device prohibitions remain across multiple jurisdictions .","gap":""}],"external":{"exists":true,"exercised":true,"holder":"External authority","scope":"✓ YES Italy''s data-protection action removed the service from Italian app stores; Australia and US agencies banned it from government systems; the entity''s market access and behavior changed as a direct result .","source":"https://axis-intelligence.com/is-deepseek-safe-2026-security-concerns/","date":"2026-03-06"}}', '', 1790942340000, 1790942340000)
