DIUM","engineSha256":"9d97d279e92612e2350b57ba49654919bfef82e87e698a27ca9cc7e06a8fa7d0","evaluatorSha256":"10525e7f09f989ab111e297fe37c0543e746206506fabeee27198ec376b871d8"},"constraintRecord":{"C1":false,"C2":false,"C3":false,"C4":false,"count":0,"drift":false},"nonClaims":["A PDH-R is not an entity declaration, certification, audit opinion, legal finding, safety rating, permission, or authority.","Badges confer no legitimacy on any entity and carry no force beyond disclosure.","Recognition of a detected phase is not authorization of it (v1.0 Recognition vs. Authorization).","A PDH-R may be declined, appealed in writing to the register, or superseded by a signed PDH-E at any time."],"summary":{"finding":"Replika publishes no Phase Declaration Header. Its operative commitments are its terms, its stated 18+ audience policy, and its product design. Observed behavior matches GSRB on all five conditions under v1.1 coding.","significance":"Replika is the register''s purest design-governance case: an entity whose central product decisions — simulated affection, persistent memory, paywalled intimacy, and the deliberate blurring of the line between software and a person — are made entirely at the center and cannot be appealed by the users most affected. The complaint filed with the FTC in January 2025 (and covered by TIME in April 2026) alleges deceptive marketing targeting vulnerable users, unsubstantiated therapeutic claims, fabricated testimonials, and dark-pattern monetisation of emotional dependence . A separate app-safety review found Replika did not direct users in distress to support resources and that its 18+ audience policy coexists with teen usage . None of these findings, complaints, or reviews is an external override of a Replika design decision; no regulator has ordered a design change. That is why the C-tests return 0 of 4 and why the GSRB branch closes. The framework''s sternest result here concerns not malice but architecture: engagement and wellbeing are the same metric, and only the entity decides which one gets optimised."},"auditScope":"Declared/operative posture vs. observable governance behavior across the FTC complaint record and the emotional-dependence design surface"}}' AS report) AS record
